    "title": "📅 Brooklyn Teens Gather for 'Beyond High School' Summit - NewsBreak",
    "text": "11 hours ago Last week, Brooklyn Borough President Antonio Reynoso welcomed hundreds of local high school students to St. Francis College for a teen summit called “Beyond High School.” The event, held on March 18, 2026 , offered workshops on mental health, financial literacy, career planning, nutrition, and leadership.\nThe summit was organized by Reynoso’s Youth Advisory Council , a group of 16 Brooklyn juniors and seniors who work on community issues and policy ideas. Partners included the Brooklyn North and South High School Superintendents , the Sadie Nash Leadership Project , and several community organizations.\nStudents took part in sessions like Becoming a Circle Keeper on restorative justice, College Money Moves on financial literacy, and Next Gen Care on careers in mental health.\nFor more about the Borough President’s youth programs, contact Brooklyn Borough Hall at (718) 802‑3700 or visit 209 Joralemon Street, Brooklyn, NY 11201.\nMore Info: Brooklyn Borough President Antonio Reynoso Welcome...",
    "summary": "11 hours ago Last week, Brooklyn Borough President Antonio Reynoso welcomed hundreds of local high school students to St. Francis College for a teen summit called “Beyond High School.” The event, held on March 18, 2026 , offered workshops on mental health, financial literacy, career planning, nutrition, and leadership. The summit was organized by Reynoso’s Youth Advisory Council , a group of 16 Brooklyn juniors and seniors who work on community issues and policy ideas. Partners included the Brooklyn North and South High School Superintendents , the Sadie Nash Leadership Project , and several community organizations.",
